Source-data-for-review/dataset1/read me for dynamic experiment.txt
(1) Dynamic experiment comprises a total of 36 test sequences, with the testing conditions configured as detailed in Table S3.

(2) Filename "data_array_1_01" represents the first test of test sequence 1, while "data_array_1_02" denotes the second repeated test of test sequence 1. Other filenames follow this naming convention accordingly.

(3) Sheet labeled "backdata" represents the comprehensive data record of the entire process for a test sequence.

(4) The remaining sheets represent four impedance tests conducted during a single NEDC test procedure.


Source-data-for-review/dataset1/read me for fault experiment.txt
(1) Fault experiment comprises a total of 35 test sequences, with the testing conditions configured as detailed in Table S2.

(2) Sheet labeled "backdata" represents the comprehensive data record of the entire process for a test sequence.

(3) Remaining sheets represent the results of five consecutive impedance spectrum tests.

(4) Designation "EIS_01" corresponds to the first impedance spectrum test. Subsequent designations follow this naming convention accordingly.


Source-data-for-review/dataset1/read me for orthogonal experiment.txt
(1) Orthogonal experiment comprises a total of 69 test sequences, with the testing conditions configured as detailed in Table S1.

(2) Sheet labeled "backdata" represents the comprehensive data record of the entire process for a test sequence. 

(3) Remaining sheets correspond to impedance spectrum measurements conducted at various current densities.

(4) Sheet titled "eis_02_1" represents the first impedance spectrum measurement conducted at a current density of 0.2 A/cm². Other sheets are named following the same convention.


Source-data-for-review/dataset2/read me.txt
(1) This dataset comprises a total of 69 test sequences, with the testing conditions configured as detailed in Table S1.

(2) Sheet labeled "backdata" represents the comprehensive data record of the entire process for a test sequence. 

(3) Remaining sheets correspond to impedance spectrum measurements conducted at various current densities.

(4) Sheet titled "eis_02_1" represents the first impedance spectrum measurement conducted at a current density of 0.2 A/cm². Other sheets are named following the same convention.

(5) Due to incomplete recording of partial time-domain data in file "test_04," the input for impedance spectrum prediction at current densities of 1.0 and 1.3 A/cm^2 was generated by replicating the operating conditions corresponding to 10,000 Hz from sheets "eis_10_x" and "eis_13_x" to a duration of 180 seconds.


Source-data-for-review/dataset3/read me.txt
(1) The folders "impedance_data" and "test_process_data" contain impedance spectrum and all recorded time-domain data during testing, including individual cell voltage data.

(2) Impedance spectrum of the stack were measured under different air stoichiometry, operating temperature, inlet pressure, and fault conditions, with specific operational parameters detailed in Tables S4 and S5.

(3) To maintain consistency with dataset 1 and dataset 2 during transfer learning, the dew point temperature was replaced with the inlet temperature as the input for impedance spectrum prediction.

(4) For certain testing conditions, impedance spectrum were measured twice and labeled as "first" and "second." Additional measurements under load shedding conditions were marked with a "load_shedding" identifier.

(5) Through multi-channel acquisition accuracy calibration, the correspondence between impedance measurement channels and CVM (Cell Voltage Monitoring) channels was established as follows:
Impedance cell2 corresponds to CVM Group 1 (Channels 1–10),

cell4 to Group 2,

cell1 to Group 3,

cell3 to Group 4,

cell5 to Group 5,

cell11 to Group 6,

cell8 to Group 7,

cell10 to Group 8,

cell13 to Group 9,

cell7 to Group 10. 

Source-data-for-review/dataset4/read me.txt
(1) All impedance test data within the folder comprehensively covers the test conditions listed in Table S6. However, time-domain test data at 0.4 A/cm² under varying air humidity and coolant temperature conditions were not utilized for impedance spectrum prediction due to incomplete recording.

(2) The numerical identifiers (Num) in folder names correspond to the test numbers specified in Table S6.

(3) The folder naming convention follows these rules:

"400_RH_20a" denotes impedance spectrum testing at 20% air humidity and 400 mA/cm² current density;

"400_Air_1_9a" represents impedance measurements at an air stoichiometric ratio of 1.9 and 400 mA/cm² current density;

"800_cT_72c" indicates impedance testing at a coolant temperature of 72°C and 400 mA/cm² current density;

"400_pre_55a" refers to impedance spectrum measurements under an air inlet pressure of 55 kPa and 400 mA/cm² current density.
Other folder names follow an analogous convention.

(4) The suffixes "a00" to "a11" in impedance spectrum filenames correspond to specific cell locations within the stack:

a00: Entire stack impedance

a01: Cell 1

a02: Cell 2

a03: Cell 6

a04: Cell 9

a05: Cell 12

a06: Cell 15

a07: Cell 18

a08: Cell 21

a09: Cell 24

a10: Cell 28

a11: Cell 29

Source-data-for-review/read me.txt
(1) This repository contains all raw files relevant to impedance spectrum testing, including not only the impedance spectrum of the membrane electrode assembly (MEA) and stack but also time-domain data recorded during testing, such as voltage, current, temperature, and flow rates.

(2) The dataset is divided into four subsets: dataset 1 is designated for base model training, while datasets 2, 3, and 4 are utilized for validation of transfer learning in model adaptation.

(3) The extracted predictive input features and corresponding impedance spectrum are documented in the dataset files within the code repository.

